The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR). This vulnerability arises because the API design allows users to directly access images via their identifiers (`imageId`) without implementing proper access control mechanisms. If the `imageId` is predictable or not sufficiently protected, unauthorized users could potentially guess or enumerate valid IDs to access images they are not authorized to view. This lack of robust authentication or authorization checks can lead to unauthorized access to sensitive or private data.

